<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">loot</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">loot</ansi> command takes everything you're entitled to
from a corpse - all its items and any gold - in a single action.

To take just one thing, use <ansi fg="command">get</ansi> with the corpse as
the source. The word "from" is optional, and <ansi fg="command">all</ansi> works too:
<ansi fg="command">get sword from wolf corpse</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">get sword wolf corpse</ansi>, or
<ansi fg="command">get all wolf corpse</ansi>. Use <ansi fg="command">look wolf corpse</ansi> to see what
it holds first.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">loot wolf corpse</ansi>      Take all loot from the wolf's corpse.
  <ansi fg="command">loot wolf</ansi>             Same - the corpse name is matched loosely.
  <ansi fg="command">loot corpse</ansi>           Loot the corpse in the room.

You can only take what belongs to you. A fresh kill is yours to loot
first; after a short while an unlooted corpse opens up to anyone in
the room. In a party, who gets what follows your party's loot rules --
see <ansi fg="command">help party</ansi>.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help get</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help party</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inventory</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help item-names</ansi>
